TzD (task #75): next_active_class steps between sched classes.
Each sched class (stop, dl, rt, fair, ext, idle) is a separate object;
only the linker script (SCHED_DATA) lays them out back to back between
__sched_class_highest and __sched_class_lowest.  With CONFIG_SMP=y,
put_prev_task_balance starts from prev->sched_class and class++ walks
past the end of that object into the next one (kc2d traps the read of
->balance in kernel/sched/core.c).  The compiler cannot know two objects
are adjacent, so the step is taken through the linker array instead.
--- a/kernel/sched/sched.h
+++ b/kernel/sched/sched.h
@@ -2519,6 +2519,11 @@
  */
 static inline const struct sched_class *next_active_class(const struct sched_class *class)
 {
+#ifdef __TZD__
+	/* Each class is its own object; only the linker places them in one
+	 * array.  Step through that array, not past the end of one object. */
+	class = &__sched_class_highest[class - __sched_class_highest];
+#endif
 	class++;
 #ifdef CONFIG_SCHED_CLASS_EXT
 	if (scx_switched_all() && class == &fair_sched_class)
